# --- Imported backlog: the burn-down -------------------------------------------
# Every citation that did not resolve when this lane was first run (plus two that surfaced
# when #595 fixed the unmatched-backtick drop), kept so the lane could go green on the day
# it landed -- the same import .github/uncovered-guards.baseline made for 283 refusal
# sites. It is 136 lines and it is only allowed to get shorter.
#
# The shape of it, so nobody mistakes the number for a triage: all 136 are in docs/adr/, mostly
# pre-reset vocabulary in decision records ADR-0008 superseded. Not one has been read individually.
# Correcting an accepted ADR's citation may well be the wrong move -- a decision record is a record
# -- in which case the right end state for that row is a line in the section above with a real
# reason, not a correction and not this marker.
